
### 1. Get all projects
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Authorization: Basic {{username}} {{password}}


### 2. Get CSRF token
GET http://localhost:8080/api/csrf
Authorization: Basic {{username}} {{password}}

> {%
    client.global.set("csrfToken", response.body.token);
%}


### 3. Create a project
POST http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{username}} {{password}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "name": "Payment Integration Test",
  "existingRepoUrl": "https://github.com/example/existing-app",
  "incomingRepoUrl": "https://github.com/example/payment-module"
}



### 4. Get project by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects/1
Authorization: Basic {{username}} {{password}}


### 5. Get a project that does not exist
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects/99999
Authorization: Basic {{username}} {{password}}


### 6. Valid project
POST http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{username}} {{password}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "name": "CodeBridge Validation Test",
  "existingRepoUrl": "https://github.com/example/project-a",
  "incomingRepoUrl": "https://github.com/example/project-b"
}

### 7. Invalid project - empty name
POST http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{username}} {{password}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "name": "",
  "existingRepoUrl": "https://github.com/example/project-a",
  "incomingRepoUrl": "https://github.com/example/project-b"
}

### 8. Invalid project - incorrect GitHub URL
POST http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic {{username}} {{password}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "name": "Invalid URL Test",
  "existingRepoUrl": "not-a-github-url",
  "incomingRepoUrl": "https://github.com/example/project-b"
}
